<%#
    The compiled Tailwind stylesheet (Scripts/BuildTailwindCss.ts). Every page
    includes this as the last thing in its <head>, because that is where the
    Play CDN runtime put the <style> it generated: it appended it to <head>
    once the body began. So the cascade is what it was - a page's own <style>
    in <head> still comes before Tailwind and loses a tie with a utility, and
    a <style> in <body> still comes after it and wins one.

    head-basic.ejs preloads the same URL near the top of <head>, so the
    download starts long before the parser gets here. Without a build it
    loads the runtime instead, and this writes nothing.
-%>
<% if (typeof tailwindStylesheetHref !== 'undefined' && tailwindStylesheetHref) { -%>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= tailwindStylesheetHref %>">
<% } -%>
